course: dictionary
lesson: 7711
title: Camouflage in the snow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ptarmigan is a plump bird that lives in cold mountains and the Arctic. You may not know this word, but the sentences around it give clues. «Ptarmigans are birds that turn white in winter and brown in summer» tells you it is a bird, and that its colour changes with the seasons.
explain: The second sentence helps too. «They dig snow caves to sleep in because snow keeps the warmth in» shows the bird lives somewhere very cold. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A plump bird of cold places. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: The author compares the ptarmigan to swapping a summer T-shirt for a winter coat. This is camouflage: changing colour so an animal blends in with what is around it. White feathers hide it in the snow, and brown feathers hide it on the summer ground.
fact: A ptarmigan is a plump bird of the grouse family.
fact: Ptarmigans live in cold mountains and the Arctic, including Scotland, Canada, Alaska and Scandinavia.
fact: In winter its feathers turn white; in summer they turn brown.
fact: Camouflage means colouring that helps an animal blend in with its surroundings.
fact: The plural can be ptarmigan or ptarmigans, so both are correct.
exercise: «Ptarmigans are birds that turn white in winter and brown in summer.» What is a ptarmigan? | A fish that lives in the sea | A small tree on the mountain | *A plump bird of the grouse family | A warm winter coat
exercise: Why does the ptarmigan turn white in winter? | To find food in the summer | To keep dry in the rain | *To blend in with the snow | To look bigger to other birds
exercise: «The arctic fox and the ptarmigan turn white for the snow and brown for the summer ground.» What does camouflage mean? | Shouting loudly to warn others | A kind of snow cave | Running very fast to escape | *Colouring that helps an animal blend in with its surroundings
test: Where do ptarmigans live? | In the middle of big cities | *In cold mountains and the Arctic | In hot deserts | Under the sea
test: Which two animals in the lesson change colour with the seasons? | The fish and the frog | *The arctic fox and the ptarmigan | The bear and the wolf | The owl and the robin
exam: «They dig snow caves to sleep in because snow keeps the warmth in.» Why do ptarmigans dig snow caves? | To grow bigger feathers | To hide treasure from other animals | *To keep warm while they sleep | To catch fish from the snow
